I'm giving a contributed talk on Meta-Harness at the CAISconf Workshop on AI Agents for Discovery in the Wild. My talk starts at 10:05 if you're here.

@Yoonholeee asks how we can autonomously improve LLM harnesses on problems humans are actively working on. Addressing this requires solving a long-horizon credit-assignment problem over all prior code, traces, and scores.

Meta-Harness is a method for optimizing harnesses end-to-end. The workshop is part of the inaugural ACM CAIS 2026, focusing on evaluation, deployment, and systems infrastructure for AI agents in real-world discovery.

